data": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 0, "created": 1793986200000, "id": "2118757808615367070", "video": {"preview": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2118741221866897408/img/crptiHc1SJGrj10A.jpg", "mpeg": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2118741221866897408/pl/hL6EbqLszii8ojQx.m3u8?v=503", "aspectRatio": [16, 9], "heightRatio": 56, "type": "video/mp4", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2118741221866897408/vid/avc1/480x270/eI75aeG1r96ccMtC.mp4"}, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2066254089756061697/MGnZGljz_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Fireside Alpha", "username": "firesidealpha"}, "content": "Data centers in Loudoun County, Virginia: \u201cWe get $1.2 billion a year in local tax revenue, about 40% of all of our tax revenue...on 3% of our land\u201d\n\nBuddy Rizer, the county's economic development chief, explained how \u201cdata center alley\u201d grew:\n\n\u201cWe would have never looked at", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 1818}, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 3, "created": 1794025951000, "id": "2118924535642931420", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1046268897853227009/3ofnBY6r_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Kane \u8b1d\u51f1\u582f", "username": "kane"}, "content": "Data centers are the closest thing to a municipal money printer for funding infrastructure and schools and the slopulist political opposition is evil.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 630}}, "post_flair_text": "SAVE AMERICA", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1AToZ3EiLH", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 64, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8928597, "raw_content": "\u201casked Grok what the chances were of 90% of Texas counties flipping from red to blue in 1.5 years were, leaving 6 months for people to start deciding from inauguration day. \r\n\r\nThis was the response. \r\n\r\nOne noventrigintacentillion.\r\n\r\nThat's a 1 (one), followed by 420 zeros. 420 zeros. Even accounting for \"muh vote turnout\", this cannot be defeated. The number would still dwarf your chances for winning the PowerBall. \r\n\r\nWake up, America. You just got roofied, r\u00e5ped, and had a kidney stolen.\u201d\r\n\r\nhttps://x.com/angrybdg/status/2118381565570936988?s=46", "author": "Inga", "created": 1794052015152, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Inga", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "AI says Dems had a One noventrigintacentillion of a chance turning 90% of Texas counties blue. No wonder they want to ban ai. It exposes their fraud. ", "last_comment_created": 1794062418303, "content": "<p>\u201casked Grok what the chances were of 90% of Texas counties flipping from red to blue in 1.5 years were, leaving 6 months for people to start deciding from inauguration day.</p>\n<p>This was the response.</p>\n<p>One noventrigintacentillion.</p>\n<p>That's a 1 (one), followed by 420 zeros. 420 zeros. Even accounting for &quot;muh vote turnout&quot;, this cannot be defeated. The number would still dwarf your chances for winning the PowerBall.</p>\n<p>Wake up, America. You just got roofied, r\u00e5ped, and had a kidney stolen.\u201d</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://x.com/angrybdg/status/2118381565570936988?s=46\" target=\"_blank\">https://x.com/angrybdg/status/2118381565570936988?s=46</a></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 7, "score_up"